4. emilkowalski/skills
==========================================================================

Upstream: https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills
Pinned at: 64eb3deb9a5fbfa041faf783e0bc3fd635872e9c (imported 2026-11-23; earlier pins e8a175de on 2026-10-08 and d23d7f88 on 2026-09-14)

Sixteen skills, each a real directory in seascape-vacations-site
.claude/skills/<name>, declared in .agents/skills-divergence.json:

  animate, animation-performance, animation-vocabulary, apple-design, ask-emil,
  break-ui, choreograph, emil-design-eng, find-animation-opportunities, gestures,
  improve-animations, learn-taste, mobile-native, prototype, remove-animations,
  review-animations.

Upstream's other four are left out, because this site is web-only and takes no
component library: animate-expo, ask-sonner, pick-ui-library, write-swift.

Invocation differs from upstream's (delta 4). Only emil-design-eng and
mobile-native, the two that were here before 2026-11-23, are listed to the
model and may load on a matching task. The other fourteen are not listed: one
loads when a person types its name, or when an agent opens its file. CLAUDE.md
sends agents to ask-emil's map, which names the other fifteen by task. What an
agent may do once a skill has loaded is set by delta 2's note, not by how the
skill loaded. emil-design-eng is the one craft skill site design work requires
(docs/agents/rules/design.md); the rest are optional. Repo design docs
(DESIGN.md) win over every one of them on motion, brand, type and copy.
`npm run audit:skills` can flag the fourteen directories added 2026-11-23 as
unused at first: read their recorded use on or after 2027-02-23 before
retiring any of them again.

Deltas from the upstream files at the pin. Reapply each one after a re-import.
scripts/enforcement/emil-skills.test.js fails when delta 1, 2, 3, 4 or 7 is
dropped and when emil-design-eng loses its description or review format
(delta 5). The repo's file-size gate fails when delta 6 is dropped. Nothing
checks emil-design-eng's agents/openai.yaml.

1. The "Initial Response" block is removed from the thirteen SKILL.md files
   that have one (all but ask-emil, gestures and learn-taste), because an agent
   loading the skill mid-task with no question would answer with that greeting
   and nothing else.
2. One note sits under the title of all sixteen SKILL.md files, whichever
   libraries a skill's text names, so the thirteen that site issue #1041
   counts as assuming an animation library are all covered. It says that
   DESIGN.md decides which motion ships, that the site's own tokens are used
   in place of a custom property an example names, and that the library
   examples (Motion, GSAP, Sonner, Vaul) are reference for other projects. It
   also says the
   skill adds no authority: an agent edits files, starts a server or
   dispatches a subagent only when its task covers that, follows AGENTS.md,
   CLAUDE.md and DESIGN.md as instructions, and keeps fixtures, prototypes and
   plans out of src/, which publishes. learn-taste's note adds that this
   repository is public: the dated comment it writes under a rule publishes
   the words it quotes, so the report shows each comment exactly, and nothing
   from a transcript goes into a file except the design correction itself.
3. Six skills name one of the four left out (animate, animation-performance,
   ask-emil, gestures, mobile-native, prototype). Their note adds that those
   four are not installed and a step that sends an agent to one is skipped.
4. Listing. Claude Code lists every skill that may load on its own, in each
   session, inside one budget the repo's own skills share
   (code.claude.com/docs/en/skills, "Skill descriptions are cut short"). In
   the sessions that made this import the budget was already spent: some of
   the repo's own skills were listed by name only. So the ten added skills
   that upstream leaves listed carry `disable-model-invocation: true` here,
   as upstream's ask-emil, learn-taste, prototype and review-animations
   already do, and the import adds nothing to the listing: the two listed
   descriptions total 897 characters against 898 before. Descriptions are
   upstream's, except that emil-design-eng keeps this repo's and mobile-native
   drops its React Native clause. Listing one of the fourteen again means
   removing that line and raising the ceiling in the test, and it takes
   listing room from the repo's own skills.
5. emil-design-eng keeps this repo's review format (one Before / After / Why
   table, without upstream's wrong-format sample), and its agents/openai.yaml,
   which is this repo's file and not an upstream one.
6. Three sections moved whole into a file beside SKILL.md, so each SKILL.md
   passes the repo's file-size gate. apple-design "Design foundations" went
   to FOUNDATIONS.md: a changed file stays under 20,000 bytes.
   emil-design-eng "Spring Animations" went to SPRINGS.md and "The Sonner
   Principles" to SONNER.md: that SKILL.md was already over the limit, and
   the gate lets such a file shrink but never grow, so its ceiling is its
   size at the last commit. A pointer to the file stays where each section
   was.
7. improve-animations/PLAN-TEMPLATE.md: upstream keeps its outer code fence
   open with four zero-width spaces before the inner fences. Here the outer
   fence has four backticks and no hidden character.

History: the 2026-09-14 adapted emil-design-eng (explicit-only, rewritten body)
was later replaced by upstream's text, because the skills are meant to fire on
ordinary design and UI work. From 2026-10-25 to 2026-11-23 only
emil-design-eng and mobile-native were kept, at e8a175de.

Re-import by copying the sixteen folders from upstream at a new pin into the
site repo's .claude/skills/, reapplying the deltas above, updating the pin
here, and keeping their entries in .agents/skills-divergence.json. Where
upstream's apple-design or emil-design-eng text has grown, move another whole
section beside SKILL.md (delta 6). Before the
new text lands, have someone with no part in the import read it for
instructions that act without being asked, withhold an answer, override the
repo's rules or reach outside the repo: it is third-party text that agents
will follow. This attribution and license travel with the skills.

